  ("48 The indefinite article" 0.0905 0.2809 0.0492 0.0683 0.0679 0.0154 0.0046 0.3458 0.0248)
  ("4.1.8 Omission of un/una after other verbs" 0.0920 0.5881 0.0825 0.1033 0.1033 0.0208 0.0068 0.3188 0.0541)
  ("Spanish does not use un/una after a number of verbs such as tener ‘to have’, comprar ‘to" 0.0920 0.9082 0.1110 0.1275 0.1274 0.0165 0.0096 0.2199 0.0681)
  ("buy’, sacar ‘to take/draw out’ (with cinema tickets, etc. ‘to buy’ or ‘to book’), buscar ‘to look" 0.0920 0.9080 0.1275 0.1440 0.1439 0.0165 0.0070 0.3000 0.0435)
  ("for’, llevar ‘to wear’, haber ‘there is/are’, when their direct object is a noun referring to things of" 0.0920 0.9081 0.1440 0.1605 0.1604 0.0165 0.0050 0.3230 0.0365)
  ("which one would normally have or carry only one: umbrella, pen, nanny, valet, cook, hat, etc." 0.0920 0.9081 0.1605 0.1770 0.1770 0.0165 0.0059 0.3247 0.0530)
  ("Omission is normal when the object is something typical or expected. As the NGLE 15.13e points" 0.0920 0.9082 0.1770 0.1935 0.1934 0.0165 0.0042 0.3890 0.0821)
  ("out, one would say María tiene perro ‘María has a dog’, but María tiene una tortuga ‘María has a" 0.0920 0.9081 0.1935 0.2100 0.2098 0.0165 0.0055 0.3643 0.0335)
  ("tortoise’." 0.0920 0.1672 0.2100 0.2265 0.2265 0.0165 nil 0.2423 0.0752)
