  ("(1) Español and andaluz are type 1 adjectives and have a feminine in -a: española, andaluza, but" 0.0920 0.9080 0.8179 0.8344 0.8342 0.0165 0.0069 0.2574 0.0225)
  ("other adjectives ending in -z or -l belong to type two, e.g. feroz ‘ferocious’, natural." 0.0919 0.7836 0.8345 0.8509 0.8508 0.0165 0.0048 0.3262 0.0448)
  ("(2) Eleven adjectives that end with -or and have a comparative meaning are type 2, i.e. they have" 0.0919 0.9081 0.8631 0.8796 0.8794 0.0165 0.0047 0.3463 0.0225)
  ("no separate feminine form. These are (singular-plural):" 0.0919 0.5570 0.8796 0.8961 0.8961 0.0165 0.0048 0.3317 0.0217)
  ("anterior – anteriores previous" 0.1092 0.3469 0.9076 0.9241 0.9240 0.0165 0.0048 0.2555 0.0621)
  ("exterior – exteriores outer" 0.1092 0.3130 0.9241 0.9406 0.9405 0.0165 0.0048 0.2318 0.0599)
  ("inferior – inferiores lower/inferior" 0.4995 0.7783 0.9076 0.9241 0.9240 0.0165 0.0048 0.3200 0.0578)
